\description{
Internal helper: Calculate AAPC results for one fitted group.

The 6.1.0 executable uses the EmpQ2 endpoint rule described by Kim et al.
(2022), with final limits based on the residual median and 5.189 times the
unscaled MAD. Observed extremes at or beyond those limits receive the
\code{2 * IQR / n} extension. The preliminary log-log fence in the executable
is overwritten before interpolation and does not affect the final limits.

Joinpoint 6.1.0 uses a 624-word generator with a legacy seed expansion and
the standard MT19937 twist.  Keeping it local avoids changing R's global RNG
state and makes the EQ stream reproducible across R sessions.

These unexported functions implement the validation, grid search, model
selection, permutation testing, coefficient inference, APC/AAPC
calculation, and empirical-quantile resampling used by the public
\code{\link[=joinpoint]{joinpoint()}}, \code{\link[=calc_apc]{calc_apc()}}, and \code{\link[=calc_aapc]{calc_aapc()}} functions. They are documented
for maintainers and are not part of the stable user-facing API.
}
\details{
The segmented-regression and grid-search implementation follows Hudson
(1966), Feder (1975), and Lerman (1980). The permutation-test helpers follow
Kim et al. (2000), with truncated sequential Monte Carlo stopping based on
Fay et al. (2007). The BIC-family scores follow Kim et al. (2009), Kim and
Kim (2016), and Kim et al. (2022), with the formulas documented by the NCI
Joinpoint Help System. APC/AAPC inference and empirical-quantile resampling
follow Clegg et al. (2009), Kim et al. (2017), and Kim et al. (2022).
}
